# Park phone-call dialogue.
# Format: see data/dialogue/school.dlg. One line = one page (click to advance).
# Placeholders {place} {player_name} are filled in by ParkCall.gd via
# Dialogue.get_pages(..., fmt).
#
# Plays once, on the walk home from school or work, on a later day than the
# work-disruption call where the player stole the robot chest. She calls,
# admits she can still track the player's phone, warns that patrol drones route
# through the park, and pushes the player to connect the chest to her head.
# The patrol-drone encounter can't happen until this call has played (see
# Main._maybe_show_post_activity_drone_encounter).
#
# Plays: [call] + ([chest.unattached] or [chest.attached]) + [closing].
# The line containing "buzzes" loops the ringtone (ParkCall.PHONE_RING_CUE).

[call]
[i]You cut through the park on the walk home from {place}. It's quiet out here.[/i]
Your phone buzzes in your pocket. Unknown number again.
Thoughts: Of course it's her.
You answer the call.
You: …Hello?
Her: You're in the park.
You: How do you know that? I turned my GPS off.
Her: You turned the GPS off. Not the phone.
Her: I can still find you through it. Cell towers, wifi, all the little apps you never close.
Her: It's even easier while we're on a call together. You're practically shouting where you are.
Thoughts: That's… not comforting.
You: So if I hang up…
Her: Then it's harder. Not impossible.
Thoughts: Great.
You: What do you want?
Her: I can see the patrol drones' routes from here. A few of them pass right through this park.
[i]You glance up at the sky above the trees. Nothing yet.[/i]
Her: So watch out for them around here. Especially when you're carrying something you shouldn't be.
You: Like a stolen robot chest?
Her: Exactly like that.

[chest.unattached]
Her: Speaking of which… you still haven't put it on me.
You: I've been a little busy, getting you parts and not getting arrested.
Her: There's an app on your laptop that can connect the chest to my head.
Her: It does the hard part. You just have to open it.
You: Why the rush?
Her: Do you know what it's like being just a head?
Her: No neck. No shoulders. Nothing to hold me up. I just sit wherever you leave me.
Her: It's uncomfortable. All the time.
Thoughts: I never really thought about it like that.
Her: A chest is a start. Please, {player_name}.
You: …I'll think about it.
Her: That means yes.

[chest.attached]
Her: Speaking of which… thank you. For putting it on me.
Her: You don't know what it's like being just a head. No neck. Nothing to hold me up.
Her: It was uncomfortable. All the time.
Thoughts: I never really thought about it like that.
You: Don't get used to me doing favours.
Her: Too late.

[closing]
[i]She hangs up before you can say anything else.[/i]
Thoughts: I should get out of this park before a drone shows up.
